# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
# QA-100 journeys gate (tests/run-installed.sh qa100): one line per qa-*.yaml / qa100-*.yaml journey.
#   journey | needs | expect | why
# journey: file name in tests/wolvm/journeys without .yaml.
# needs (comma list; a journey runs only when the gate's --have covers every one):
#   live         the VM boots the 0.12.1 ISO (live session, account `live`, uid 1000)
#   installed    the VM boots an installed 0.12.1 disk
#   iso-install  the journey installs itself: a fresh VM with the ISO (and the autoinstall words in its header)
#   account:NAME a desktop account on the installed disk (alice = Alice Liddell/curiouser, aliceliddell,
#                bob/curiouser, tester/tester123); account:none = no account yet (Setup Assistant)
#   network      the guest reaches the internet (Store, update, module download)
#   displays:N   at least N heads (wolvm new --displays N)
#   audio        HDA sound cards (wolvm new --audio 2); no-audio = no card at all (the wolvm default)
#   s3           S3 sleep offered (wolvm new --s3) for the suspend/wake steps
#   usb          USB hot-plug through QMP (plug/unplug steps; an image file next to the run)
#   disk-edit    the host edits the stopped VM's disk first (wolvm disk-edit, qemu-nbd + sudo)
#   tpm, secureboot, drive (an extra raw disk, --drive), ssh (--ssh), release-0120 (the 0.12.0 ISO)
# expect: pass, or fail:<id> = the registry id (.claude/v012/qa100/BUGS.md, registry 4) the journey is
#   expected to FAIL on today (rel/0.12.1). Ids written <report>:<local id> come from hunter reports
#   that registry 4 has not merged yet (crash-surface, devices-r2, kernel-boot, kernel-boot-r2,
#   data-safety, launcher-notify, upgrade-path, plugins-maker-r2).
#   fail:<id>@<steps> pins the journey step numbers (as `wolvm journey` prints them) whose assertion
#   is the bug: the gate says XFAIL only when the first failed step is one of them, INFRA otherwise.
#   fail:<id>@visual: no step asserts the bug (shots, saved output, probes that always pass): REVIEW.
#   No suffix: any failure is XFAIL (not pinned yet).
qa-auth-two-requests | installed,account:alice | fail:QA-HUNT-1@visual | Cancel prints "Incorrect password" (confirmed on 0.12.1); QA-QAF-6 two requests also present
